\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Literature context of the 5$\sigma $ trigger thresholds, in total power (\S  \ref  {sec:background}). \emph  {(a)}\nobreakspace  {}EIRP against distance. Blue: this survey, deepest window per star (88{} stars, 1.30--39.63\,pc; filled: Class\nobreakspace  {}A, fine-channel; open: Class\nobreakspace  {}B, coarse-channel); orange: \citet  {Enriquez2017}; aqua: \citet  {Margot2023}; violet: \citet  {Mason2024}; left-edge ticks: deepest per-target limits of \citet  {Price2020}. Grey dotted: EIRP $\propto d^{2}$ at constant received flux. Green dashed: the Arecibo 2.38-GHz EIRP benchmark, a power scale only (\S  \ref  {sec:benchmarks}). \emph  {(b)}\nobreakspace  {}Native channel width against observing frequency for the same windows and programmes: resolutions differ by ${\sim }10^{7}$, so the panels must be read together and a lower EIRP here does not imply greater sensitivity to a hertz-wide carrier. Plotted values are nominal $5\sigma $ triggers: they exclude both the $\times 2.29$ median spectral-response correction and the $\times 1.41$ available from the individual parallel hands, so a transmitter comparison carries a further $\times 3.2$ against this survey's curve at the median response, more in the tail.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:context}{{1}{3}{Literature context of the 5$\sigma $ trigger thresholds, in total power (\S \ref {sec:background}). \emph {(a)}~EIRP against distance. Blue: this survey, deepest window per star (\NStars {} stars, \DistMin --\DistMax \,pc; filled: Class~A, fine-channel; open: Class~B, coarse-channel); orange: \citet {Enriquez2017}; aqua: \citet {Margot2023}; violet: \citet {Mason2024}; left-edge ticks: deepest per-target limits of \citet {Price2020}. Grey dotted: EIRP $\propto d^{2}$ at constant received flux. Green dashed: the Arecibo \ArecGHz -GHz EIRP benchmark, a power scale only (\S \ref {sec:benchmarks}). \emph {(b)}~Native channel width against observing frequency for the same windows and programmes: resolutions differ by ${\sim }10^{7}$, so the panels must be read together and a lower EIRP here does not imply greater sensitivity to a hertz-wide carrier. Plotted values are nominal $5\sigma $ triggers: they exclude both the $\times \HanFacMed $ median spectral-response correction and the $\times \PolGain $ available from the individual parallel hands, so a transmitter comparison carries a further $\times \DebitCombined $ against this survey's curve at the median response, more in the tail}{figure.1}{}}
