\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Left: the selection funnel. The three denominators the text keeps apart are the catalogued population, the 168-entry ALMA-covered work list, the ${\sim }115$ stars a public field genuinely contains, and the 88{} searched. Right: the decision flow from spectral window to disposition. The 512-control comparison is a candidate-generation screen, and the gates in italic are where a crossing can leave the chain.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:funnel}{{2}{5}{Left: the selection funnel. The three denominators the text keeps apart are the catalogued population, the \NCensus -entry ALMA-covered work list, the ${\sim }\NGenuinelyCovered $ stars a public field genuinely contains, and the \NStars {} searched. Right: the decision flow from spectral window to disposition. The \NCtrl -control comparison is a candidate-generation screen, and the gates in italic are where a crossing can leave the chain}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces What this survey sampled in frequency. Each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance and labelled alternately on the left and right axes, coloured by nominal EIRP$_{5\sigma }$, with line weight distinguishing the fine-channel (Class\nobreakspace  {}A) from the unresolved-spectral-excess (Class\nobreakspace  {}B) channelisation; the upper panel counts systems per gigahertz of sky frequency. The coverage is narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited: 45{} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, with summed window bandwidth $6.5\times $ the union. The union is the frequency coverage; the summed bandwidth is the integrated search effort, and the two answer different questions (Scope of the constraints, \S  \ref  {sec:method}).}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:waterfall}{{3}{5}{What this survey sampled in frequency. Each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance and labelled alternately on the left and right axes, coloured by nominal EIRP$_{5\sigma }$, with line weight distinguishing the fine-channel (Class~A) from the unresolved-spectral-excess (Class~B) channelisation; the upper panel counts systems per gigahertz of sky frequency. The coverage is narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited: \UnionIntervals {} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, with summed window bandwidth $\GrossOverUnion \times $ the union. The union is the frequency coverage; the summed bandwidth is the integrated search effort, and the two answer different questions (Scope of the constraints, \S \ref {sec:method})}{figure.3}{}}
