\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The four stage-1 spatial outliers, with the evidence dispositioning each. $T_\star $ is the search statistic at the stellar position (Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {eq:tstar}) and `ring max' the largest of that window's 512{} control statistics; $\nu _{\rm  cross}$ is the crossing channel, which differs from the window centre by up to 0.85\,GHz here, and $S_{\rm  peak}=T_\star \sigma $ is the peak flux density in one native channel. $\Delta \nu $ and $\Delta v$ give the topocentric offset of that channel from the nearest \emph  {laboratory} rest frequency of the masked species, signed so that a negative value places the observed channel \emph  {below} the rest frequency, that is, redshifted relative to it. The mask of \S  \ref  {sec:linecost} changes no row, and the HD\nobreakspace  {}48370 row is the limiting case, a near-tie of rank dispositioned by velocity coincidence with independently published emission.}}{13}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:flagged}{{6}{13}{The four stage-1 spatial outliers, with the evidence dispositioning each. $T_\star $ is the search statistic at the stellar position (Eq.~\ref {eq:tstar}) and `ring max' the largest of that window's \NCtrl {} control statistics; $\nu _{\rm cross}$ is the crossing channel, which differs from the window centre by up to 0.85\,GHz here, and $S_{\rm peak}=T_\star \sigma $ is the peak flux density in one native channel. $\Delta \nu $ and $\Delta v$ give the topocentric offset of that channel from the nearest \emph {laboratory} rest frequency of the masked species, signed so that a negative value places the observed channel \emph {below} the rest frequency, that is, redshifted relative to it. The mask of \S \ref {sec:linecost} changes no row, and the HD~48370 row is the limiting case, a near-tie of rank dispositioned by velocity coincidence with independently published emission}{table.6}{}}
