\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The survey rescored under both repairs. ``Survives'' is the largest stellar debit $m(0)$, in units of each window's own control scale, at which the star still exceeds every detrended control; it is a property of the window and assumes neither debit. For reference the conservative debit is 0.15$\,\sigma $ and the debit that centres the calibration-sample rank distribution is 0.32$\,\sigma $, and a window survives whichever debit is smaller than its entry. No window is added by either repair.}}{14}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:repaired}{{8}{14}{The survey rescored under both repairs. ``Survives'' is the largest stellar debit $m(0)$, in units of each window's own control scale, at which the star still exceeds every detrended control; it is a property of the window and assumes neither debit. For reference the conservative debit is \RmDebitCons $\,\sigma $ and the debit that centres the calibration-sample rank distribution is \RmDebitCal $\,\sigma $, and a window survives whichever debit is smaller than its entry. No window is added by either repair}{table.8}{}}
