\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Selection function of the searched sample against a volume-limited reference census: Gaia\nobreakspace  {}DR3 sources with $\varpi >0$, $\sigma _\varpi /\varpi \le 0.1$ and $1/\varpi \le 40$\,pc (17566 objects, of which 8594 carry a \texttt  {teff\_gspphot} estimate, 49 per cent), against the 88 stars with at least one searched window. Temperatures are available for 52 of the 88 (all 88 matched to the 168-entry ALMA-covered census, 58 by exact name; 52 of those matches carry a temperature), so the temperature panel is normalised over classified objects only. ``Ratio'' is the sample column fraction over the census column fraction; $>1$ is over-representation.}}{20}{table.11}\protected@file@percent }
